#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380192 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49147c48-3c79-59ef-85df-0ae687ad910c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380194} {:answer/id #uuid "43c20240-428f-5295-ac13-745401af8941" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380195} {:answer/id #uuid "b39fbfd4-ff69-5b93-9537-86630db7fb44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380196} {:answer/id #uuid "5b1511a1-0592-5e16-ae3d-355dbe352c92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380197} {:answer/id #uuid "aed5ce7a-ce77-563e-a120-802fb7c3c0e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b39fbfd4-ff69-5b93-9537-86630db7fb44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380196} :answer-field/id #uuid "51cbf961-880f-5565-ab09-ae794ec61fcf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "401ba6bc-fa27-5ba0-acab-8c53d45558b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-127873" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-3,1,-2⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ -3{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}-2{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b379fd-7d70-5e49-8081-a3b64f84134e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,4⟩=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380208} {:answer/id #uuid "0d2c1c27-eb96-5b3b-9be4-85fc3ed5d870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,-4,3⟩=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380209} {:answer/id #uuid "18790217-0164-5be5-8309-2e02c079a999" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,4,4⟩=23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380210} {:answer/id #uuid "56439333-b485-5577-b3fc-2b0a4fb30508" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,4⟩=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380211} {:answer/id #uuid "0677a85c-be73-579f-a4cd-3b2a328033da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩=23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0677a85c-be73-579f-a4cd-3b2a328033da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩=23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380212} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ea1771e-337a-53ba-af67-134749c7dc53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5fb6c451-3fd1-5933-bfd5-1dcab52c2777" :question/math-academy-id "q-127927" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(1,-2,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(4,1,-3)$ and $B(7,-3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨1,-2,3⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(4,1,-3)$ and $B(7,-3,1)$, we can find a vector that is parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨7,-3,1⟩-⟨4,1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨3,-4,4⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ & =⟨1,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24d09d6d-587a-5131-bf7b-17c4a5299f8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-6,4,5⟩=28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380215} {:answer/id #uuid "97b1a154-e6ea-5ad5-bc67-985ac790249f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨6,5,-4⟩=24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380216} {:answer/id #uuid "c19bf435-7bb8-561f-ba12-0c791dd434be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨4,-5,6⟩=-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380217} {:answer/id #uuid "6397ae12-fbfa-5ef2-932b-49e1d8b15ea1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩=-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380218} {:answer/id #uuid "facf8c4b-8e3d-5a24-a63e-b12fc172190e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-5,6,4⟩=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6397ae12-fbfa-5ef2-932b-49e1d8b15ea1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩=-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380218} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c8d44ee-444f-5365-a1c8-4d6392e75dfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0063bd61-9495-5b7f-ae6d-384a92c58a15" :question/math-academy-id "q-127948" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(-3,2,1)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+6t \\\\ y=3-5t \\\\ z=-2+4t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨-3,2,1⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+6t \\\\ y=3-5t \\\\ z=-2+4t\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨-1,3,-2⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨6,-5,4⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨6,-5,4⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨6,-5,4⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ & =⟨-3,2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
